BUG TO FIX (src/plugin/timezone/index.js, the `proto.tz` instance method, currently lines 55-59):

  proto.tz = function (timezone) {
    const target = this.toDate().toLocaleString('en-US', { timeZone: timezone })
    const diff = (this.toDate() - new Date(target)) / 1000 / 60
    return d(target).utcOffset(localUtcOffset - diff, true)
  }

`toLocaleString` has no milliseconds, so when the instance has a non-zero millisecond part `diff` is fractional (e.g. 420.00205 for ts 1401624000123 in America/Los_Angeles). That fractional value is stored as `$offset`, so `format('Z')` renders garbage such as '-07:0.00205' instead of '-07:00' (and `utcOffset()` returns a non-integer). Fix by rounding:

    const diff = Math.round((this.toDate() - new Date(target)) / 1000 / 60)

Make ONLY that one-line change (keep the rest of the file exactly as it is, including the `if (typeof input !== 'string')` branch that was added earlier in `d.tz`). Do not modify any other file.

VERIFY:
1. Write /dayjs/test/zz_tmp_tz.test.js that, for zones ['America/Los_Angeles','America/New_York','Europe/London','Asia/Tokyo','Asia/Kolkata','Australia/Sydney','America/St_Johns','UTC'] and timestamps [1401624000000, 1401624000123, 1401624000500, 1401624000999, 1401624000001, 1401638400123], compares dayjs(ts).tz(zone) against moment(ts).tz(zone) on format(), format('Z'), format('ZZ'), utcOffset() and valueOf(). Print every mismatch as `zone | ts | field | dayjs=.. | moment=..` and print the total mismatch count (must be 0 after the fix). Also print the dayjs value of format('Z') for ts=1401624000123 in America/Los_Angeles before and after your change (run the test once before editing to capture the broken output).
2. Run: cd /dayjs && npx jest test/plugin/timezone.test.js --coverage=false 2>&1 | tail -20 (all 14 tests must pass; the container TZ is UTC).
3. Run the FULL suite before and after your edit: cd /dayjs && npx jest --coverage=false 2>&1 | tail -20. Baseline in this container (TZ=UTC) is 56 suites / 524 tests all passing; report any test that passed before and fails after.
4. DELETE /dayjs/test/zz_tmp_tz.test.js afterwards and confirm `git status --porcelain` shows src/plugin/timezone/index.js modified only by the expected changes.

